   "narration": {
    "en": "The story is by James Herriot, a veterinary surgeon. He tells of Tricki Woo, a small Pekingese dog owned by the wealthy Mrs Pumphrey. Mrs Pumphrey pampered Tricki with too many rich foods and sweets, so he grew fat, lazy and breathless."
   },
   "actions": [
    {
     "do": "draw",
     "target": "p0",
     "at": 0.1
    },
    {
     "do": "write",
     "target": "n0",
     "at": 0.2
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "d3",
   "narration": {
    "en": "Herriot saw at once that Tricki was only overweight and lacked exercise. He decided the only way was to take Tricki away from her house. He took Tricki to his own surgery, with Mrs Pumphrey and the staff weeping and throwing coats at the car."
   },
   "actions": [
    {
     "do": "draw",
     "target": "p1",
     "at": 0.1
    },
    {
     "do": "write",
     "target": "n1",
     "at": 0.2
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "d4",
   "narration": {
    "en": "At Herriot's place Tricki was put on a strict diet and played with other dogs, so he became lean and lively. After a few days he went home healthy, and Mrs Pumphrey called it a triumph of surgery, though no surgery was done."
   },
